EXT. LIFE RAFT - SOUTHERN OCEAN - DAWN

A yellow canopy bobbing on a swell the color of slate. Fog lies in the troughs. The sea has gone, for the first time in nine days, almost still.

CAPTAIN HAAKON LUNDQVIST, 60s, a beard crusted with salt, sits at the hatch with a flare gun across his knees. MBEKI NTULI, 30s, the first mate, bails with a plastic cup, steady as a metronome. LUCIANA FARIAS, 20s, the cook, huddles in a foil blanket, lips cracked. PIP, 16, the cabin boy, lies asleep with his head in her lap.

HAAKON
It's flat.

MBEKI
It's flat.

LUCIANA
Is that good?

HAAKON
It means the storm's gone.

MBEKI
It means the storm's behind us.

LUCIANA
Is that different?

MBEKI
Ask me tomorrow.

HAAKON
Water?

LUCIANA
Half a cup each. I measured.

HAAKON
Split Pip's.

MBEKI
He's nine days younger than the rest of us.

HAAKON
Give him less, then.

LUCIANA
No. I'm giving him more.

HAAKON
Luciana --

LUCIANA
He told me his mother's name. Last night. He thought I was asleep. He kept saying it. Over and over. Adelheid. Adelheid.

MBEKI
Captain, the boy's all right.

HAAKON
The boy's fine.

LUCIANA
You keep saying that like it's a prayer.

HAAKON
It's a log entry.

MBEKI
It's both.

Pip stirs. Murmurs. Luciana strokes his forehead. All three wait for him to settle.

HAAKON
(low)
Mbeki. Last night. Did you hear it?

MBEKI
The engine?

HAAKON
Not an engine.

LUCIANA
What are you two talking about?

MBEKI
A low sound. Like a drum, far off.

HAAKON
I thought I dreamed it.

MBEKI
We didn't both dream it.

LUCIANA
Could it be a ship?

HAAKON
Ships don't sound like that.

LUCIANA
Then what?

HAAKON
Whales. Or ice. Or --

He stops. The fog parts. In the trough ahead, a wall of white rises, hundreds of feet high, glittering.

MBEKI
Iceberg.

LUCIANA
It's beautiful.

HAAKON
It's moving toward us.

MBEKI
Everything moves toward us, Captain.

Pip sits up. Rubs his eyes. Looks at the berg and the three adults, all staring, none speaking.

PIP
Is it breakfast?

Luciana laughs, ragged, helpless, near tears. Mbeki lowers his bailing cup. Haakon lifts the flare gun, aims into the gray sky, and fires.

A red star blooms above them. Four faces turn up to it, lit crimson, silent.
